  "keyworded random slopes (≥1)" = "R already has this (RE-01/RE-02, folded into the matched 'grouping level x unit' row above, both `covered`); a naming/granularity difference, not a gap owed to R -- if anything Julia is behind here",
  "uncorrelated slope (r double-bar / uncorrelated re)" = "no register evidence for a distinct `||` uncorrelated-slope grammar on either side; both packages lack it, so this is not a Julia-ahead gap",
